<section class="sec dark gutter" id="approach" aria-labelledby="ap-h" style="margin-top:110px">
  <div class="wrap approach">
    <div class="ap-l">
      <span class="lbl"><b>[ 03 ]</b> Approach</span>
      <h2 id="ap-h">The agent does the typing. I do the thinking.</h2>
      <p>Every report goes through the same six steps. The repetitive ones go to an AI agent connected to the model. The judgement stays with me.</p>
      <div class="legend2"><span class="who me">Me</span><span class="who ai">Agent</span><span class="who both">Together</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><span class="n">01</span><div class="body"><h3>Brief</h3><p>Who reads it, what they decide with it, and the three numbers that matter.</p></div><span class="who me">Me</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="n">02</span><div class="body"><h3>Wireframe</h3><p>The layout is agreed before Power BI Desktop opens.</p></div><span class="who both">Together</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="n">03</span><div class="body"><h3>Model</h3><p>Measures, relationships and descriptions written straight into the semantic model.</p></div><span class="who ai">Agent</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="n">04</span><div class="body"><h3>Scaffold</h3><p>Pages and visuals generated as report files from the wireframe and theme.</p></div><span class="who ai">Agent</span></div>
      <div class="step key"><span class="n">05</span><div class="body"><span class="h tl"></span><span class="h tr"></span><span class="h bl"></span><span class="h br"></span><h3>Design pass</h3><p>Spacing, hierarchy, zero padding. The part that makes it stop looking like Power BI.</p></div><span class="who me">Me</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="n">06</span><div class="body"><h3>Review and handover</h3><p>Best-practice checks, documentation, and a file your team owns.</p></div><span class="who both">Together</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
